# Line-ending policy.
#
# This repo is edited on Windows (core.autocrlf=true) and executed on a Linux
# GPU server. Without an explicit policy a shell script can reach the server
# with CRLF endings, where bash fails on the invisible carriage return:
#
#     ./run.sh: line 2: $'\r': command not found
#
# Pinning eol=lf on everything executable removes that entire class of bug,
# regardless of what each contributor's autocrlf happens to be set to.

# Normalise all text files in the repository to LF.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Scripts that run on Linux MUST be LF, no exceptions.
*.sh      text eol=lf
*.bash    text eol=lf
*.sbatch  text eol=lf
*.py      text eol=lf

# Windows-only helpers keep CRLF, since that is what cmd.exe expects.
*.bat     text eol=crlf
*.ps1     text eol=crlf

# Never touch binaries -- newline conversion corrupts them.
*.pdf     binary
*.png     binary
*.jpg     binary
*.gguf    binary
*.safetensors binary

# Datasets are text, but keep diffs readable rather than exploding on every
# regenerate: they are large and machine-generated.
*.csv     text eol=lf diff
*.json    text eol=lf diff
